title: Reshuffle the Cabinet
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and reshuffle_timer <= 0 and months_in_office >= 6
on-arrival: reshuffle_timer = 12; month_actions += 1

= Reshuffle the Cabinet

Chancellor: [+ chancellor +]. Employment: [+ employment_secretary +]. Industry: [+ industry_secretary +]. The Cabinet is [+ cabinet_dry +]% dry.

[? if cabinet_revolt >= 5 : The wets in Cabinet are close to open revolt. ?]

- @purge: Sack the wets and promote the believers.
- @bring_back: Bring the wets back into the economic departments.
- @loyalists: Promote loyal managers.
- @easy_discard

@purge
view-if: wets_purged = 0
subtitle: The Cabinet becomes yours. The sacked will not go quietly.
on-arrival: wets_purged = 1; cabinet_dry += 35; cabinet_dry = 95 if cabinet_dry > 95; chancellor = "Howe"; chancellor_dry = 1; employment_secretary = "Tebbit"; employment_dry = 1; industry_secretary = "Joseph" if industry_dry = 0; industry_dry = 1; tebbit_advisor = 1; wet_dissent += 15; wet_strength -= 5; dry_dissent -= 8; cabinet_revolt = 0; rebellion += 2
achievement: purge

Ian Gilmour, Christopher Soames and Mark Carlisle are sacked. Jim Prior is moved to Northern Ireland. Norman Tebbit, Nigel Lawson and Cecil Parkinson come in. Gilmour tells the cameras outside Number 10 that it does no harm to throw the occasional man overboard, but it doesn't do much good if you're steering full speed ahead for the rocks.

@bring_back
view-if: cabinet_dry >= 40
subtitle: Calms the wets, at the cost of the radical programme.
on-arrival: wets_purged = 0; cabinet_dry -= 25; chancellor = "Pym" if chancellor_dry = 1 and cabinet_dry < 40; chancellor_dry = 0 if cabinet_dry < 40; employment_secretary = "Prior"; employment_dry = 0; wet_dissent -= 12; dry_dissent += 10; cabinet_revolt -= 3; rebellion -= 2

The economic departments go back to the consensus men. [? if chancellor_dry = 0 : Even the Treasury changes hands. ?]

@loyalists
on-arrival: loyalist_dissent -= 6; cabinet_revolt -= 2; rebellion -= 1

Party managers and safe pairs of hands fill the middle-ranking jobs. Nobody is thrilled, and nobody is furious.
